---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="Why Flash Was Great" filename="articles/flash.htm">
  <p><a href={`${base}articles/`} class="back-link">← Back to Articles</a></p>

  <h1>Why Flash Was Actually Great</h1>

  <p><em>Published: January 15, 2024</em></p>

  <hr />

  <p>
    Let's talk about something that's been on my mind lately: <strong>Macromedia Flash</strong>.
    Yes, that Flash. The one that got killed off, blamed for security holes, and replaced
    by HTML5. But here's the thing — Flash was actually incredible.
  </p>

  <h2>The Creative Explosion</h2>

  <p>
    In the early 2000s, Flash was everywhere. Band websites had elaborate animated intros.
    Games like <em>QWOP</em> and <em>Line Rider</em> captured millions of hours of our time.
    Homestar Runner became a cultural phenomenon. Newgrounds was the YouTube before YouTube.
  </p>

  <p>
    Flash democratized animation and interactive content. Anyone with a copy of Flash MX
    could create something magical. You didn't need to know complex programming — the
    timeline-based animation was intuitive and visual.
  </p>

  <h2>The Web Had Personality</h2>

  <p>
    This is what I miss most. Flash websites had <em>character</em>. Each site was a unique
    experience. You'd wait for the loading bar to fill up, then be transported to someone's
    creative vision. Sounds would play. Things would animate. It felt alive.
  </p>

  <blockquote>
    "The web used to be weird, and that was beautiful."
  </blockquote>

  <p>
    Compare that to today's web: endless scrolling feeds, cookie banners, the same Bootstrap
    layouts everywhere. We gained performance and accessibility, but lost a lot of soul.
  </p>

  <h2>What We Can Learn</h2>

  <p>
    I'm not saying we should bring Flash back (please don't). But we <em>can</em> bring
    back the spirit:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>Add meaningful animations that delight users</li>
    <li>Design unique experiences, not templates</li>
    <li>Include easter eggs and surprises</li>
    <li>Let your personality shine through</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    This website is my attempt at capturing that magic with modern tech. CSS and JavaScript
    give us the animation power. The tools have never been better — we just need to use
    them creatively.
  </p>

  <p>
    Long live the spirit of Flash! ⚡
  </p>

  <hr />

  <div class="fp-nav-bar">
    <a href={`${base}articles/`} class="fp-nav-btn">◀ Back to Articles</a>
  </div>
</Layout>
